---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'agreement', label: 'Agreement' },
  { id: 'services', label: 'Services and client agreements' },
  { id: 'using-the-site', label: 'Using the site' },
  { id: 'our-content', label: 'Our content' },
  { id: 'estimates', label: 'Estimates and examples' },
  { id: 'what-you-send', label: 'What you send us' },
  { id: 'third-parties', label: 'Third-party services' },
  { id: 'disclaimers', label: 'Disclaimers' },
  { id: 'liability', label: 'Limitation of liability' },
  { id: 'indemnity', label: 'Indemnity' },
  { id: 'governing-law', label: 'Governing law' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
const host = Astro.site?.host;
const mail = `mailto:${site.email}`;
const state = site.governingState;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that apply when you use the Own Your eCommerce website."
  updated="2026-09-10"
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="agreement">Agreement</h2>
  <p>
    These terms apply to your use of {host} (the "site"), which is operated by {site.legalName} ("we",
    "us", "our"). By using the site, you agree to these terms and to our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    If you don't agree, please don't use the site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="services">Services and client agreements</h2>
  <p>
    The site describes the custom eCommerce design, development, hosting setup, and support services we
    offer. Any work we do for you is governed by a separate written agreement, such as a signed proposal or
    statement of work, which sets out the scope, price, timeline, and who owns what. If that agreement
    conflicts with these terms, the agreement wins. Nothing on the site is an offer you can accept just by
    using it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="using-the-site">Using the site</h2>
  <p>You're welcome to use the site to learn about our services and to contact us. You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>use the site in a way that breaks the law or infringes anyone's rights;</li>
    <li>try to gain unauthorized access to the site, our systems, or anyone else's data;</li>
    <li>disrupt the site, for example by overloading it or introducing malware;</li>
    <li>scrape or copy the site in bulk, or use it to build a competing service;</li>
    <li>send spam or submit false or misleading information through our forms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="our-content">Our content</h2>
  <p>
    The site's text, design, graphics, logo, and code belong to us or our licensors and are protected by
    intellectual property laws. You may view the site and share links to it, but you may not copy, modify,
    or republish its content without our written permission, except as the law allows.
  </p>
  <p>
    Other company and product names mentioned on the site, such as Shopify, Wix, Helcim, FedEx, UPS,
    QuickBooks, and Xero, are trademarks of their respective owners. Mentioning them doesn't mean they
    endorse us or that we're partners.
  </p>

  <h2 id="estimates">Estimates and examples</h2>
  <p>
    Savings estimates, fees, timelines, uptime figures, and other numbers on the site are general
    information based on typical projects and publicly available provider pricing. They aren't quotes or
    guarantees. Your actual costs and results depend on your business and will be set out in your proposal.
  </p>
  <p>
    The dashboards, customer names, orders, and figures shown on the site are illustrative examples, not
    real customers or data.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-you-send">What you send us</h2>
  <p>
    You're responsible for the information you send us, and you confirm you have the right to share it.
    Please don't send confidential information until we've agreed how it will be protected, for example
    under a non-disclosure agreement. Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle
    personal information.
  </p>

  <h2 id="third-parties">Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    The site links to and relies on services run by other companies, such as payment processors, shipping
    carriers, hosting providers, and our form and font providers. We don't control them and aren't
    responsible for their content, policies, or availability. Your use of them is governed by their own
    terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disclaimers">Disclaimers</h2>
  <p>
    We work hard to keep the site accurate and available, but it's provided "as is" and "as available". To
    the fullest extent the law allows, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including warranties
    of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. We don't promise that the
    site will be error-free, uninterrupted, or free of harmful components.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent the law allows, {site.legalName} isn't liable for any indirect, incidental,
    special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue, or data, arising from your
    use of the site. Our total liability for any claim relating to the site is limited to US$100. Some
    places don't allow these limits, so they may not all apply to you. This section doesn't change the
    liability terms of a signed client agreement.
  </p>

  <h2 id="indemnity">Indemnity</h2>
  <p>
    If you misuse the site or break these terms, you agree to cover the reasonable costs, including legal
    fees, that we incur as a result, to the extent the law allows.
  </p>

  <h2 id="governing-law">Governing law</h2>
  {state ? (
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the State of {state} and applicable US federal law, without
      regard to conflict-of-law rules. Any dispute relating to the site will be handled exclusively in the
      state or federal courts located in {state}, and you and we consent to their jurisdiction.
    </p>
  ) : (
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the US state in which {site.legalName} is organized and
      applicable US federal law, without regard to conflict-of-law rules. Any dispute relating to the site
      will be handled exclusively in the state or federal courts located in that state, and you and we
      consent to their jurisdiction.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top shows when they last
    changed. If you keep using the site after an update, you accept the new terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms? Email <a href={mail}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
